592186235486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ecd7d48-e192-56ba-a9eb-6c4280135677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ecd7d48-e192-56ba-a9eb-6c4280135677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234667} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1bfa42a-8d4e-593c-aa9b-c50e784fddb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235263}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "615b21ea-17f4-5ce5-8433-316c3df76ca0" :question/math-academy-id "q-167787" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}}-x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x)\n$$\n\nThe order of this differential equation is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "We have the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}}-x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}},$ which has order $4.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22ac80f9-d1a9-57b5-8a75-ee4e690886f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.ty